title: "Sperm whale coda vowels hold steady through whole bouts"
abstract: "A pre-registered test on the public labels behind the sperm whale 'vowel' papers. Neighbouring codas switch vowel about a fifth as often as chance predicts, and the same whale's vowel mix changes between tag deployments. The vowel behaves like a state of the moment, not a choice made coda by coda. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
